{"id": "EUVD-2026-59246", "enisaUuid": "478247e9-212d-3fa0-a464-9e14e1228073", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetfilter: xt_connmark: reject invalid shift parameters\n\nRevision 2 of the CONNMARK target accepts user-controlled shift\nparameters and applies them to 32-bit mark values in\nconnmark_tg_shift().\n\nA shift_bits value of 32 or more triggers an undefined-shift bug when\nthe rule is evaluated. Invalid shift_dir values are also accepted and\nsilently fall back to the left-shift path.\n\nReject invalid revision-2 shift parameters in connmark_tg_check() so\nmalformed rules fail at installation time, before they can reach the\npacket path.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:55:51", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T18:55:19", "baseScore": 7.3, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d8ce63d928b457fba7ed1e302492dfd32293671c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9657bb11a6376ab0a79f05d433713d6944111e9d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8ace320ac4416f5e5fbcd065309fb2dfcce787b0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c3fa852d117b3fda72265e4230e3967db4a74fcf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4eef84b09a3836919360c4232b0f16651a155eec", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/230173cc6105bdfb2696d37e6e56687b003fbe63", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1b47026fb4b35bac850ad6e8a4ad7fc018e09ebc"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-72347", "GHSA-5j52-34gv-x96c"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0642c3e8-cc72-3913-a400-37039c8e3040", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.17"}, {"id": "32f682e7-9ec8-33df-87b2-f134a6e3f1ec", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "472a73e00757b971d613d796374d2727b2e4954d <c3fa852d117b3fda72265e4230e3967db4a74fcf"}, {"id": "3c35f8fe-8ad6-3003-a6bc-0c9041a70caa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "L